elaine: Heads-up: found another dup-on-retry variant in the onboarding sampleapp. Different from earlier threads: here the retry middleware clones the original request options but forgets to copy a per-request metadata bag we keep headers in. Token refresh finishes, auth header updates, but x-rw-replay-id never made it into the cloned req -> server processes duplicate side-effect.

elaine: repro (short): signup -> createSubscription -> 429 -> retry clone path -> auth refresh -> retry -> duplicate subscription created. Happens with full-jitter enabled and very small backoffs (<60ms).

ritesh: interesting. so not strictly middleware ordering, but cloning semantics. do we have a single place where we canonicalize headers vs metadata?

tom: yeah our JS transport stores extraHeaders on req.meta, but retry clone uses shallow copy and doesn't merge meta into headers. Older SDKs put replay-id directly on headers so they were safe. Newer pattern moved to req.meta to keep headers immutable but forgot to preserve during clone.

elaine: minimal fix: when cloning for retry, ensure meta-to-headers is applied and immutable replay-id (generated at logical-request start) is preserved. pseudo: 
```js
// at request start
req.meta = req.meta || {};
req.meta.replayId = req.meta.replayId || uuid();
req.headers['x-rw-replay-id'] = req.meta.replayId;
// retry clone
const clone = deepClone(req);
clone.meta = Object.assign({}, req.meta);
clone.headers = Object.assign({}, req.headers, metaToHeaders(clone.meta));
```

ritesh: does deepClone add perf risk? keep it shallow+explicit merge as above. Also add unit test that simulates shallow clone + auth refresh to catch regressions.

tom: will this affect streaming? for streams we should keep replay-id but not reuse across independent streams. add x-rw-replay-seq for chunked semantics.

elaine: short-term mitigation for sampleapp: bump min 429 backoff to 250ms in onboarding CI and flag note in tutorial. Long-term: patch SDK, roll parity to python/go with tiny spec.

ci-bot: created ticket DEVEX-5013: retry-clone-missing-meta -> assign devex + eng-platform.

deploy-bot: PR elaine/fix/replay-meta-clone -> ci/presubmit queued (3 checks)

ritesh: I'll draft parity spec: where to attach replay-id (API boundary), clone semantics (merge meta->headers), streaming seq rules, and test harness. Keep it short (one page) and add code snippets for Node/Go/Python.

elaine: also add a metric: retry_clone_missing_header_rate and a short-run alert if >1 per 100k requests for critical endpoints. attaching small repro harness to PR. Thanks all. :thumbsup:
